 "contents": "unpressurised open driving station: rubber deck tread tiles (cut around the seat pedestals / controller columns / console), 4 alu cage handrails with black grips on graphite clamps to the roll-cage posts, 4 LED task-light bars under the top cross rails, graphite tool / sample stowage box (off-white lid, 2 black tie-down straps, 2 alu latches, yellow label), 2 small touchscreens on the console top",
 "notes": [
  "unpressurised open station: no wall / ceiling panels, end walls or pressure vessel; the 'IML' is the crew envelope box inside the roll cage (iva note)",
  "cage clamps (graphite) and the rear LED-bar housings reach up to 40 mm (corner, 28-30 mm per axis) out of the envelope box onto the roll-cage tubes (inner faces x +-1.12, rear rail z -1.07) by design: the cage is outside the envelope (containment flags = these only)",
  "seats, hand controllers and console are exterior meshes (kept); deck tiles are cut around their footprints (10 mm)",
  "2 small touchscreens sit on top of the exterior console (tilted to the crew)",
  "egress: no hatches -> seat exit to an outboard stand-up column (0.40 m), 0.18 m inboard of the open side; side opening (envelope side face) clear z -1.05..~+0.68 (front post) x floor..top rail (1.87 m) = ~1.7 m wide, minus the exterior hand-controller column (x +-0.9..1.0, z -0.15..-0.05, up to y 0.05) which splits it into 0.9 m (aft) and 0.72 m (fwd, back to the console face z 0.675) at foot level",
  "R3 re-export: seat / camera nodes lowered 0.095 m (node_seat y -0.325, node_camera y 0.425); seated feet now rest on the deck tread tiles (0.015 m to the envelope floor, as the iva note states)",
  "R3 re-export: the IML GLB is no longer a plain box: it cuts out the exterior seats (x +-0.30..0.80, z -0.66..-0.14), hand-controller columns (x +-0.90..1.00, z -0.15..-0.05) and console (x +-1.0, z 0.50..0.85) (vol 6.90 vs box 7.82 m3); deck-tile cutters follow these footprints (console cut moved from z 0.665 to 0.49)"
 ],
